{"message":"I verified your identity and checked your profile. Your Gold Rewards Card application is not showing as an active card yet, so the Gold Account’s reduced $5,000 minimum does not currently apply. The standard Gold Account minimum is $10,000.

Because you have $5,000 available, I did not open the Gold Account—you would not meet its current minimum-balance requirement, and opening it could leave the account out of good standing. No savings account was opened and no funds were transferred.

Once the Gold Rewards Card is approved and active, I can recheck eligibility and open the Gold Account with your $5,000, subject to the account’s other terms."}

{"message":"Yes. The best documented personal option that does not depend on the pending card is the **Silver Plus Account**. Its documented APY is 3.0% for balances below its higher tier, with a 0.025% relationship bonus when eligible; it also has no paper-statement fee. Your existing Light Blue checking account does not provide a linked-savings boost.

Because you said you will fund it yourself later, please note that the account must be funded within 30 days of opening or it will be closed. I will not transfer money from your checking account now.

Please confirm that you want me to open the **Silver Plus Account** with no initial transfer."}
